  "metadata": {
    "title": "SpaceX Rally Lifts Valor's Stake to Nearly $97 Billion After 43% Gain",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "This article first appeared on GuruFocus.\nAntonio Gracias has emerged as one of the biggest winners from SpaceX's (NASDAQ:SPCX) market debut, as Valor Equity Partners' stake in the rocket company was worth almost $97 billion as of Monday's close. The Chicago-based private equity firm's position has helped lift Gracias' estimated net worth to $24.4 billion, according to the Bloomberg Billionaires Index, which is valuing his fortune for the first time. SpaceX shares have gained 43% since trading began in New York on Friday, bringing sharper attention to Gracias' long-running bet on Elon Musk's companies.\nGracias' relationship with Musk stretches back decades and has possibly been central to Valor's access to some of Musk's most valuable ventures. Valor became the first institutional investor in Tesla (NASDAQ:TSLA) in 2005, invested in SpaceX three years later, and backed Neuralink and the Boring Co. Gracias also extended Musk a short-term loan in 2008 when his companies were facing bankruptcy, while Musk invested $2 million into each of Valor's first two funds. By the time Gracias left Tesla's board in 2021, he had built a stake currently worth more than $1.6 billion after adjusting for a 2022 stock split.\nValor insiders own about a quarter of the firm's assets under management, but they hold 64% of Valor Space Holdings, which owns a SpaceX position worth about $18.8 billion, according to an April 2026 filing. Bloomberg credits Gracias with a personal SpaceX stake worth $16.8 billion through Valor funds, plus $3.3 billion in non-SpaceX insider assets and a Valor ownership stake worth about $2.7 billion. Valor's SpaceX funds have already recorded more than $39 billion in gains since the start of the year, and future carried interest distributions could possibly add further upside when the funds eventually return capital to investors.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "This article first appeared on GuruFocus.",
      "Antonio Gracias has emerged as one of the biggest winners from SpaceX's (NASDAQ:SPCX) market debut, as Valor Equity Partners' stake in the rocket company was worth almost $97 billion as of Monday's close. The Chicago-based private equity firm's position has helped lift Gracias' estimated net worth to $24.4 billion, according to the Bloomberg Billionaires Index, which is valuing his fortune for the first time. SpaceX shares have gained 43% since trading began in New York on Friday, bringing sharper attention to Gracias' long-running bet on Elon Musk's companies.",
      "Gracias' relationship with Musk stretches back decades and has possibly been central to Valor's access to some of Musk's most valuable ventures. Valor became the first institutional investor in Tesla (NASDAQ:TSLA) in 2005, invested in SpaceX three years later, and backed Neuralink and the Boring Co. Gracias also extended Musk a short-term loan in 2008 when his companies were facing bankruptcy, while Musk invested $2 million into each of Valor's first two funds. By the time Gracias left Tesla's board in 2021, he had built a stake currently worth more than $1.6 billion after adjusting for a 2022 stock split.",
      "Valor insiders own about a quarter of the firm's assets under management, but they hold 64% of Valor Space Holdings, which owns a SpaceX position worth about $18.8 billion, according to an April 2026 filing. Bloomberg credits Gracias with a personal SpaceX stake worth $16.8 billion through Valor funds, plus $3.3 billion in non-SpaceX insider assets and a Valor ownership stake worth about $2.7 billion. Valor's SpaceX funds have already recorded more than $39 billion in gains since the start of the year, and future carried interest distributions could possibly add further upside when the funds eventually return capital to investors."
